  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}y & =c \\\\ xy(y-x) & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=-1,$ the level curve is $xy(y-x)=-1,$ which is not a parabola. So, I is false.\n\n- If $c=0,$ the level curve is $xy(y-x)=0,$ which gives the $y$-axis, the $x$-axis and the line $y=x.$ So, II is true.\n\n- If $c=1,$ the level curve is $xy(y-x)=1,$ which is not the line $y=2x.$ So, III is false.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
